april is sexual assault awareness month  and the goal of this month is to shed  light on the stories of survivors the  group signs of hope which is a rape  crisis center is a major resource for  victims in the community during the  pandemic the group says they saw a  dramatic increase for counseling  services in 2021 they met with 450  people at hospitals for sexual assault  exams and handled more than 14 000  hotline calls and website visits they  continue to partner with las vegas metro  police to train hospitality workers on  how to spot and prevent predatory  behavior  it really is an opportunity to take a  lot of the  stigma and shame that survivors often  feel and just  begin talking more about this issue that  affects so so many people that we often  don't discuss and kind of keep in the  dark we also want all survivors out  there to know that we are here to  support them  signs of hope will kick off the month  with a community resource fair today  april 5th it's from 4 pm to 7 p.m in the  courtyard of the organization's office
 

